Recommended preparation order
For your Java Developer interview preparation, study these areas first:
Priority	Topics	Questions
1	Entity lifecycle, persistence context, dirty checking	21–40
2	Relationships, lazy/eager loading, N+1	41–80
3	Transactions and Spring integration	96–115
4	Caching and performance optimization	116–150
5	Locking and concurrency	151–165
6	JPQL and Spring Data JPA	166–180
7	Production scenarios	211–225
My recommendation: For a 10-year candidate, prepare each important topic in four parts: definition, internal working, practical code, and a production scenario. Interviewers often ask follow-up questions that test whether you understand the consequences of your design decisions.